    rdfs:comment "Compiled by Anton Wiklund with the help of AI."@en ,
                 "Sammanställd av Anton Wiklund med hjälp av AI."@sv ,
                 "Licensing: the theory, questions, options and notes are the course's own text, written from the statutes and the sources listed; no question bank, book or app was used. Statutes and agency regulations carry no copyright (upphovsrättslagen 9 § första stycket). Facts from the EU reports (CC BY 4.0) are restated in the course's own words and credited below, so the course stays CC0. The sign pictures are linked, not copied, from Wikimedia Commons, under Transportstyrelsen's permission."@en ,
                 "Selection: 16 chapters following what the theory test for license B covers (TSFS 2012:43 4–7 §§), basics first: each sign group is introduced in chapter 0 and each sign is taught again with its rule. Topics with no usable source beyond the statutes (first aid technique, drive systems and skidding, aquaplaning, eco-driving figures, crash-risk figures by experience) are kept to what the statutes say, or left out; first aid points to a first aid course."@en ,
                 "Rules as amended up to: trafikförordningen SFS 2026:1052, vägmärkesförordningen SFS 2025:268, lag (1951:649) SFS 2024:715, körkortslagen SFS 2026:469, körkortsförordningen SFS 2026:470; the other sources' dates are in their own entries."@en ,
                 "Language: the course is written in Swedish first, the language of its sources and of the test. Every other language is translated from the Swedish, never from another translation; this version has the English translation. Terms follow one glossary in both languages, Swedish following the statutes' own words."@en .

<#review-0>
    a prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "Sources and licenses"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: each source's license or legal basis, checked before use by AI agents against the source's own terms (upphovsrättslagen 9 § for the statutes and regulations; the European Commission's and the EEA's legal notices; Transportstyrelsen's permission for its sign files and each Commons file's license template, read through the Commons API). Every request used an honest User-Agent on hosts whose robots.txt and terms allow it."@en ,
                 "Outcome: only statutes, Transportstyrelsen's regulations, CC BY 4.0 reports of the European Commission and the EEA (facts restated, credited below) and sign files tagged PD-Transportstyrelsen are used. Topics with no such source are kept to what the statutes say."@en .

<#review-1>
    a prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "Facts against the statutes"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: every chapter, after it was written in Swedish: each statement in the theory, each right answer, wrong option and note, checked by an AI agent against the cited sections in the statute texts, and each sign picture's code against the current vägmärkesförordningen."@en ,
                 "Outcome: wrong or overstated rules, section numbers, options that were also right, and figures without a source were corrected or replaced, chapter by chapter."@en .

<#review-2>
    a prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "Swedish language and question design"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: every chapter's Swedish, checked by an AI agent for plain, correct Swedish in the statutes' own terms, and for questions that work both as multiple choice and as recall cards: fronts answerable without options, options alike in form, each question answerable from its step's theory, picture descriptions that do not give the answer away."@en ,
                 "Outcome: fronts, options and theory were reworded where needed; facts were left to the fact check."@en .

<#review-3>
    a prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "English translation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: the English, translated by an AI agent from the Swedish only, then checked field by field against the Swedish by another agent: meaning, numbers, section references, legal terms, American spelling, options alike in form, theory chunks matching the Swedish."@en ,
                 "Outcome: additions, omissions and imprecise terms were corrected in the English; the Swedish was not changed in this round."@en .

<#review-4>
    a prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "Across chapters"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: all questions of the 16 chapters compared by an AI agent for questions asked twice, contradictions and terms used differently; each fix then made in Swedish first and checked by a second agent against the statutes. One glossary of terms was applied to both languages."@en ,
                 "Outcome: 18 findings fixed: duplicate questions replaced (among them the tire rules, kept in chapter 3), a contradiction on how far a prohibitory sign applies resolved with the exceptions in vägmärkesförordningen 2 kap. 8 §, and terms made consistent (the statute's funktionshinder, polisen, märket, trafiksignal, plankorsning)."@en .

<#review-6>
    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-22T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "Version 2: questions that work as flip cards too (AI)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: every question of the course read by AI agents as it is later studied flip-and-grade, its front alone with no options, in Swedish and in English, for questions whose answer is one of several valid ones, that make sense only with their options or that do not ask for what the back answers; each finding put to three more AI agents, and kept when two upheld it. The questions upheld were rewritten by an AI agent in Swedish first, the English translated from the Swedish, and each revision checked by three others, for recall from the front alone, for the multiple choice (one correct option; wrong options plausible, of the same form and wrong for the new question) and for its facts against the step's theory and the cited statutes, its Swedish and its English translation, and rewritten until all three passed; the release compared with version 1 and checked by the library checker; not a human review."@en ,
                 "Outcome: of 301 questions, 2 are asked anew; 3 wrong options that no longer fitted are retired and 3 new ones added. Every chapter, step and card keeps its id."@en .

<#review-5>
    a prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "Machine checks"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: the release checked by the library's SHACL shapes, the DCAT-AP validator and its course, Markdown and curation rules (npm run library:check)."@en ,
                 "Outcome: valid."@en .

